# L §7.2: "Steps that aren't powers of ten exist in law, such as 5 Rappen (N-208) ... An ask may write any positive
# step."  "It gives money when U is a currency and the step is a whole number of minor units".  1.07 CHF to 0.05 CHF
# half-up: 1.07 / 0.05 = 21.4, the nearest multiple 21 × 0.05 = 1.05 CHF.  An integer num from round(x, 1, mode)
# is accepted as an int (here a def typed int).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit CHF: currency minor 0.01
input p: money CHF
input y: num

def nyears: int at reader
  rule base = round(y, 1, ceil)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  p = 1.07 CHF
  y = 2.1

ask q1: round(p, 0.05 CHF, half-up), nyears law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (1.05 CHF, 3)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
